cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MaplePy or Hopper, please cite the paper below and name the release you used."
title: "MaplePy: MAPLE from crystallographic information files, and Hoppe's additivity theorem tested at database scale"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Reeves-McLaren
    given-names: Nik
    affiliation: University of Sheffield
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1061-1230"
  # Pending Peter's agreement to the licence and to software authorship;
  # his ORCID goes here when he sends it.
  - family-names: Gross
    given-names: Peter
    affiliation: University of Sheffield
version: 1.4.0
abstract: >-
  MaplePy computes per-site and total MAPLE (Madelung Part of Lattice
  Energy) values from CIF files with the Ewald summation in pymatgen,
  recording where each oxidation state came from, deriving Z from the site
  multiplicities, treating disorder by mean-field charges, and flagging
  geometry that cannot carry a Madelung energy. Hopper decomposes ternary
  oxides into their binary oxides, computes the residual of Hoppe's
  additivity theorem against a 112-entry reference table, and classifies
  each structure into one of twelve codes in three tiers. This release is
  maplepy 1.4.0, running MaplePy 1.3.6 and Hopper 1.2.9.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SuperBladesman/MaplePy"
keywords:
  - crystallography
  - MAPLE
  - Madelung energy
  - lattice energy
  - additivity theorem
  - crystal structure validation
  - ICSD
  - CIF
